Halacha Four

Part Two &mdash; Sections &#x05D6;&ndash;&#x05D9;

Section Seven &middot; &#x05D6;

And this is the aspect of flour: it is impossible to make bread unless one first grinds the wheat into flour, which is ground and divided into very, very fine particles &mdash; so that the sparks are divided into very many parts, so that we can then specifically gather them and clarify them and make from them dough and bread. Then they are included in the stature of man (komat adam) through the man eating them &mdash; and they are the essential vitality and satisfaction of man: namely the sparks which are the divine vitality (chiyus Elokyus) within them, from which comes the essential satisfaction and life-force. And this is what Rashi explained regarding the creation of the first Adam: &ldquo;he kneaded the dough&rdquo; (lash es ha&rsquo;isah) (Sanhedrin 38b) &mdash; for it is all one. For the dust of the first Adam was gathered from all parts of the world, for all the sparks and all the souls were included in him &mdash; as is known. And this is the aspect of dough (isah) made from flour as mentioned &mdash; which is the aspect of Torah, the aspect of &ldquo;if there is no flour, there is no Torah.&rdquo;

And this is why the clarification of the halachos by talmiday chachamim was compared to the clarification of foods &mdash; as the Mishnah says: &ldquo;there are four types among students: a sponge, a funnel, a strainer, and a sieve&rdquo; (sefog, mashpech, mishemeres, nafah) (Avos 5:15).

And therefore the essential completion of the clarification is through the Chalah separated from the dough made of flour and water &mdash; the waters of da&rsquo;as [knowledge] and Torah drawn upon the flour. And through this one gathers and collects it and kneads it and makes dough. And then it is obligated in Chalah: to give the raishis to the Kohen who is composed of ben v&rsquo;talmid, through which the entire dough is included in the aforementioned aspect, in the aspect of Torah and da&rsquo;as, through which all the sparks ascend etc. as mentioned. And therefore Chalah is practiced even now outside the Land of Israel, because through Chalah comes the essential clarification as mentioned.

